<Layout title="Website privacy" description="How the NRTH website handles inquiry drafts, browser preferences, and basic website access.">
  <article class="legal-content"><span class="eyebrow">Website information</span><h1>Privacy.</h1><p>This page describes the NRTH public website. Individual NRTH products and services may have separate privacy information appropriate to their actual operation.</p><h2>Inquiry drafts</h2><p>The inquiry tool prepares a message in your browser. It does not submit the message to a website server. You can copy it, download it, or, when a contact address is available, open it in your email application. Sending through an email application is a separate action controlled by you.</p><h2>Your preferences</h2><p>If you change the motion setting, the website may store that preference in your browser’s local storage. Your device’s reduced-motion setting is also respected. This preference is not used to identify you or track you across websites.</p><h2>Website access</h2><p>This implementation does not include advertising trackers or analytics. Fonts and graphical assets are served with the website. The hosting provider may process technical information needed to serve requests; the final hosting arrangements should be reflected here before launch.</p><h2>Sensitive information</h2><p>Please do not include medical records, payment details, passwords, or other sensitive information in a general website inquiry.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> to prepare a question about the website or privacy.</p></article>
</Layout>
